{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>He made him ride on the high places of the earth.</b> He gave him dominion over a superior land, which is the center of the inhabited world and higher than all other lands. The sense of these verses is that He bestowed goodness and well-being upon them, and they spurned Him. And the sense of ״חלב כליות חטה״ — the fat of kidneys of wheat — is the fat of wheat; and it says ״kidneys״ (כליות) because wheat kernels resemble kidneys. And the Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted that the wheat kernels were like the kidneys of the largest ox in the generation of Shimon ben Shetach."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:53:05.622538674Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}